ies nearly all of the training core-error gain (−1.2% without it), val7 all of the validation core-error gain (+2.7% without it), and val5 about 61% of the validation MAE/L gain. Outside these cases the change is roughly neutral on core error.","Each figure comes from a single closed-loop run. Changes of about 0.01 pp in core error or tens of reads in the 5L counts may be within the perturbation noise of closed-loop feedback.","The two mechanisms were evaluated only together, so their contributions are not separated. The val2 and val5 overprediction regressions and the higher drift could come from pending_unforced over-extending write mode in write-heavy phases, or from the one-cycle precharge delay.","val7 remains a −4.8% core-level underprediction and dominates the validation mean. The candidate reduces it but does not address its cause.","The write-recovery exclusion for pre_wait was chosen from closed-loop outcomes, after the unrestricted pre_wait candidate was rejected. That choice carries some tuning risk, although validation core error and MAE/L both improve.","Only single-core cases exist in this stage, so behavior under multicore contention with the new write-mode extension is not measured."]}
